00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
ladies and gentlemen and welcome to this  virtual meeting meeting of council  all members of the council have been  invited to attend this meeting  electronically and we've received  apologies from councillors bunting  duffield minis new and shaw because of  their work commitments and also  counsellor mrs churchill  and do we have any further apologies  please uh  council councillor rigby i put it in the  chat  thank you councillor rigby i've also had  apologies from councillor kerry  any more counselors um new  walsh taylor bennett dr carr  and stennett mr mayor  um councillor jerome uh who uh will  hopefully be able to join us soon  thank you you got all those in  thank you  thank you i'm sure we all appreciate  that uh the timing makes it difficult  for some members  um moving on um can i remind everybody  when participating in this virtual  meeting to please remember to mute your  microphone when not speaking  to use the chat facility to indicate to  me if you would like to speak  and finally to leave the meeting once it  ends with a little red button  um so moving on item one announcements  it is my very sad duty to um inform  council  of the passing of former councillor  david merrill  uh mr merrill was the member for village  ward from 1983 to 1987  and for bowdoin ward from 1988 to 2008  he had a very distinguished career on  trafford council  rising in the end to become deputy  leader and was the mayor of trafford  from 1997  to 1998. so can we all just  take a moment of silence just to  remember mr merrill and his family  please thank you  thank you very much everyone um  obviously the funeral has taken place in  accordance with the current restrictions  but i have been in contact with his  family  to convey uh trafford's fondest wishes  to them  moving on um the item one leader do you  have any further announcements please  no thank you mr man thank you  item two then um i invite councillor tom  ross the executive member for finance  and investment  to introduce the report and move the  recommendations regarding the  redesignation of leisure center  refurbishment earmarked reserve  councillor ross please thank you mr  mayor um this afternoon i'm seeking  council's approval to redesignate the  leisure center refurbishment earmark  reserve  as the leisure reserve council will be  aware that restrictions to control the  spread of covert 19 were introduced in  march and required  the closure of all leisure centers the  actions to protect public health from  the virus were  crucial however the impact has caused a  considerable deterioration of trafford  ledger's trading position  last week the government announced that  indoor leisure facilities and swimming  pools will be allowed to open from the  25th of july  however the necessary requirement of  social distancing measures and an  enhanced cleaning regime  will mean that trafford leisure's  financial position will not improve  immediately  trafford leisure does not have reserves  in place and would not be able to secure  a finance from a commercial lender  trafford leisure was set up with the  council as sole shareholder and  responsible for underwriting its  financial position  therefore if traffic ledger ceased to  trade as a company the council would be  required to pick up the responsibilities  for the staffing  and other associated costs  in the light of this there is a strong  case for the council and trafford  leisure to work together to keep the  company's financial position  under review on a month by month basis  you'll be aware council agreed to  provide a loan to trafford leisure on  the braces that it was short-term  support urgently required to deal with  the immediate effects of the pandemic  restrictions  trafford leisure then approached the  council to request request a grant to  cover their projected trading deficit to  the end of the trading year  however the financial position of the  council has meant that it is not  open to us to provide a further facility  by grant or loan  what we can consider and recommend is  the redesignation of the reserve  originally earmarked to cover the risks  to income during the future leisure  centre redevelopment work  the value of this reserve is 968 000  pounds  we have sought the advice of leading  council to provide assurance as to the  lawfulness of any decision to provide  further support  to offset trafford leisure's ongoing  liabilities  that assurance has been provided in the  meantime we have employed max associates  to work with trafford leisure  to review the financial projections to  the end of the financial year  we will also be carrying out a full  review of our leisure strategy later in  the year  if the council agrees to the  recommendation in the paper payments  will only be  advanced on a month by month basis and  be subject to the approval of the  corporate director  for finance and systems i stress again  that if we do not agree to this course  of action  then the council would be request  required to pick up the responsibilities  for the staffing and other associated  costs where trafford leisure to cease  trading  thank you mr mayor i move the report  thank you councillor ross um i  understand this will be seconded by  councillor weston  councillor patel mr sorry councillor  patel  thank you mr mayor um i'd like to second  this report  um council ross has covered the  financial and legal background  uh to this report could i just please  make a few broader points about our  leisure service  the kovic crisis has had and will  continue to have a big impact on council  services  and more widely on our economy sectors  like leisure have been particularly hard  hit  and will continue to be impacted by  social distancing requirements  and more broadly by potential reshaping  of the leisure market  work continues with traffic ledger to  develop a reopening plan that maximizes  income  and reduces expenditure and we will be  working closely with trafford leisure on  a month-by-month basis to review the  support needed  this reopening plan will be communicated  publicly in the next week or so  i would like to thank trafford leisure  and council staff who have been working  with dedication and  under great pressure to protect protect  our leisure offer  it's been a very challenging and  uncertain time  offices and our partners have  demonstrated that even under such  circumstances a constructive way forward  can be found  the decision to allow more flexibility  with the allocation of this reserve is  welcome  and will help stabilize leisure services  in trafford in the short to medium term  what's needed in the longer term however  is a more sustainable leisure offer  this decision today provides us with a  breathing space which will allow us  in conjunction with our partners to  undertake an in-depth review  of what and how we deliver our leisure  services locally  just like to finish really the impact on  of the kovi crisis has really  highlighted health inequalities in  trafford  and we will continue to work closely  with partners to narrow this gap  thank you mr moon  thank you councillor patel um i haven't  had any indications that anybody wishes  to speak on this  um can anybody who does wish to do so  please  indicate on the um chapter  no there are a couple of hands mr and  the participant  got to look at hands um  whose other hands i'm sorry i can't keep  track of everyone's hands  all right councillor coggins please  thank you chair uh green group will are  happy to support this move today  um it's really important we know that  there is a strong  covert related public health argument  for keeping people as active as we can  at the moment there are very few things  we can do  to to help um to help residents of  trafford  through the next year and one of them is  to help keep people um strong and fit  and active so i think supporting our  leisure centers  and and everything else that we can do  that will support people being fit and  active  and being in the strongest condition  they can it's very important at the  moment  and my one uh word of caution is just  having read through the paper and having  read through the previous paper which i  believe went through in 2015 that was  also  actually an urgent uh piece of business  just to um  to echo cancer patel's calls for a more  sustainable leisure strategy in the long  run we  we we need to show that we really value  our leisure centers and that we have a  long-term sustainable plan so  i look forward to seeing that coming  through in in the medium term  thank you thank you very much councillor  cobbins  councillor myers please  yes thank you mr mayor um i think it's  fair to say that in view of the  um the current situation the coveted  situation  there's no real alternative to this i  think it's a  well formulated approach and i can't see  any  realistic alternative but what i would  say is in  section 17 of the report it talks about  um  the future um beyond 2021  i just wonder what plans have been made  if the financial situation  isn't any any better at that time so in  other words  we're still in a difficult situation  with with finance  bearing in mind that the council is also  in a difficult situation with finance  where will the money come to support it  because at the end of the day it's a  non-statutory function thank you mr  mayor  thank you councillor myers councillor  ross you don't have to come back to that  book do you wish to  thank you mr matt and first of all thank  you to councillor coggins for her  comments and also to  to to councillor myers in terms of um  what councilor maya says about the  replenishment of the reserves obviously  at the moment we're continuing to  press the government to recognize the  situation with leisure centers which i  know is an issue  across the country the government has  come forward with some proposals  but it's not quite clear yet that we  would be covered from them so we're in  as far as i understand it we're still in  discussions with uh with the government  about that  and we'd hope that we'd get additional  support through to um  support our leisure strategy our leisure  centres  and obviously importantly to build up  those reserves again  thank you very much councillor ross um  i've had no  further indications um so with that  um could i um take a view as to whether  this can be agreed by consensus  or is there any dissension in that  everyone happy councillor evans  consensus  mr mayor thank you councillors coggins  and new gross everyone happy yes happy  for consensus  thank you everyone uh with that um i  think we can uh  take it as it is all agreed um  and therefore the recommendations have  been approved  thank you everybody for agreeing to this  meeting at the last minute i'm sure you  agree it's um  an important subject to discuss um  before we go can i once again just thank  all members who have  contributed to helping our most  vulnerable residents over the lockdown  period  i'm sure it has been very much  appreciated i know a lot of people have  been involved  so thank you very much stay safe and  that is the end of the meeting ladies  and gentlemen

